WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.379
So far we have imported modules that

00:00:02.405 --> 00:00:05.316
already exist Now we will look at

00:00:05.342 --> 00:00:07.553
the idea of creating our own module

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:10.605
Suppose we are working on an analytics

00:00:10.632 --> 00:00:13.618
project that repeatedly calculates profit and profit

00:00:13.645 --> 00:00:16.842
margin We could write those formulas again

00:00:16.855 --> 00:00:18.750
and again in the main program but

00:00:18.776 --> 00:00:22.092
that creates repetition A better approach is

00:00:22.118 --> 00:00:24.474
to create a separate file called calculations

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.658
dot P Y Inside that file we

00:00:26.671 --> 00:00:28.974
can define functions such as calculate profit

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.000
and profit margin Then we create another

00:00:32.026 --> 00:00:35.158
file perhaps main dot P Y The

00:00:35.171 --> 00:00:37.790
main file imports the calculations module and

00:00:37.816 --> 00:00:41.145
uses those functions when needed This creates

00:00:41.158 --> 00:00:45.434
a clear separation of responsibilities The
calculations

00:00:45.461 --> 00:00:49.237
file stores reusable formulas The main file

00:00:49.263 --> 00:00:52.526
focuses on the current analysis This is

00:00:52.553 --> 00:00:55.013
useful because the main program becomes shorter

00:00:55.026 --> 00:00:57.737
and easier to read It is also

00:00:57.763 --> 00:01:01.079
easier to update the formula later If

00:01:01.105 --> 00:01:03.289
we change the calculation in one module

00:01:03.539 --> 00:01:05.618
every script that imports that module can

00:01:05.645 --> 00:01:09.276
use the updated logic A beginner-friendly rule

00:01:09.289 --> 00:01:12.053
is this When one script starts to

00:01:12.079 --> 00:01:15.092
contain many useful helper functions consider moving

00:01:15.105 --> 00:01:18.355
related functions into their own module You

00:01:18.368 --> 00:01:19.974
do not need to create a separate

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.118
file for every tiny function The goal

00:01:23.145 --> 00:01:24.697
is not to break a project into

00:01:24.724 --> 00:01:28.079
dozens of unnecessary files The goal is

00:01:28.105 --> 00:01:29.645
to group related code in a way

00:01:29.658 --> 00:01:32.053
that makes the project easier to understand
